From be094c5ff116578c192f9d58bcd95c5ea5e74b47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emil Boenke <boenkeemil@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:51:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] German by default on German-speaking systems, and bundled
 dictionaries

craft-proof now checks German (compounds included) when a German Hunspell
dictionary is found, but new documents were still written in US English on
an Austrian or German system, and no dictionary came with the program.

- new documents follow the region's German: a German interface, or an English
  one on a German-speaking system, writes de-AT / de-DE / de-CH
- a `dictionaries` folder beside the program (or in the macOS bundle's
  Contents/Resources) is searched when no dictionaries folder is set
- German (Austria) and German (Switzerland) in the Language dialog and the
  region list

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GBuDRRQePZfJwfmCbrvseN
